# Android / Gradle
#
# The Gradle wrapper JAR is intentionally NOT ignored — see the note at the
# bottom of this file.

## Build output
build/
app/build/
.gradle/
captures/
out/
release/

## Local SDK location. Machine-specific, never committed; CI resolves the SDK
## from ANDROID_HOME instead.
local.properties

## Packaged apps
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

## Signing material. Release signing is configured through GitHub Actions
## secrets; private keys and local signing properties must never be committed.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

## Android Studio / IntelliJ
#
# Ignored wholesale. Nothing in here is needed to build the project, and the
# files are rewritten constantly with machine-local paths.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.navigation/
.cxx/

## VS Code
#
# The opposite call to .idea/, because two of these files are project
# configuration rather than personal preference:
#
#   settings.json    associates *.kts with Kotlin. Without it every Gradle build
#                    file opens as Plain Text — a real, reproducible problem that
#                    a fresh clone would otherwise have to rediscover.
#   extensions.json  names the four extensions this project needs, so a new
#                    clone is not left guessing which of the dozen Kotlin
#                    extensions on the marketplace is the right one.
#
# Everything else VS Code writes into this folder is per-user or per-machine, so
# the folder is ignored and the shared files are added back.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/*.code-snippets

## Kotlin
.kotlin/

## Java
*.class
*.log
hs_err_pid*

## Lint and test output
lint-results*.html
lint-results*.xml
app/lint-baseline.xml

## Emulator and adb noise
*.hprof

## Screenshots pulled off an emulator land in a folder of this name at the repo
## root. Anchored with a leading slash so it does not also swallow
## assets/screenshots/, which is the curated set the README points at.
/screenshots/

## OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
#
# Committing the wrapper jar is the Gradle-recommended practice and is what
# makes `./gradlew` work on a fresh clone. It is a binary, so it cannot be
# generated by hand — run `gradle wrapper` once with a system Gradle and commit
# the result.
#
# CI does not depend on it: the workflow installs Gradle through
# gradle/actions/setup-gradle and calls `gradle` directly, so the pipeline is
# green with or without the jar present.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
